<h3>Cross-attention</h3>
<p>Reference PyTorch Whisper exposed decoder cross-attention weights that were unavailable through my production CTranslate2 path.</p>
<p>Attention over Friedberg's ghost interval was faint but non-zero.</p>
<p>Gerstner's region also showed weak activity, although it bordered much stronger surrounding speech and was harder to interpret cleanly.</p>
<p>The attention plot did not prove that Whisper had recognized the words.</p>
<p>It did show that the decoder was not operating over a completely empty region.</p>
